The query responsible for this particular issue:


{noformat} query CategoriesPage(
    $categoryId: String
    $beehiveLang: String
    $countryCodeRe: String
  ) {
    sections: allBeehiveSection(
      filter: { categoryId: { eq: $categoryId }, lang: { eq: $beehiveLang } }
      sort: { fields: { title: ASC } }
    ) {
      nodes {
        fields {
          route
          title
        }
        articles(limit: 5, countryCode: $countryCodeRe) {
          articleId
          fields {
            route
            title
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }{noformat}

returns 0 articles for all categories when countryCode is global i.e /xx.*xx|^xx$/.  Which is why there are no articles displayed for global.


Updating the regex to:

{{/(^|,)(${GLOBAL_COUNTRY_CONFIG.code}|${countryCode})($|,)/}}

i.e for global: {{/(^|,)(xx|xx)($|,)/}}  , this fixes the issue.




